-- FOR THE STABLE BUILD.  The smallest file that uses the time built-ins and nothing else unstable (it uses Date,
-- not YMD, and no REFUSE), so that a main build's refusal can be read as the built-ins' alone.
-- Printed by the unstable build (shelf and dev alike): 7, 9 (see f09-stable-build-temporal-only.out).
-- Printed by the main build 1.6.98: errors, "I could not find a definition for the identifier" (see
-- f09-main-build.out, written by run-findings.sh when a main build is given as L4_MAIN).
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

`GST rate` MEANS
    IF (DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE`) AT LEAST (DATE_SERIAL (Date 1 1 2024)) THEN 9 ELSE 7

#EVAL `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (Date 1 6 2023) `GST rate`
#EVAL `EVAL AS OF SYSTEM TIME` (Date 1 7 2024) (`EVAL UNDER VALID TIME` (Date 1 7 2024) `GST rate`)
